cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. Not peer reviewed. Produced by AI models under the direction of the repository owner (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md)."
title: "The pentagonal bipyramid as the unique logarithmic-energy minimiser for seven points on the sphere: an unreviewed Lean 4 warrant (Conjecture 1 of Armentano et al.)"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23086382"
version: "v2.8"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/thomson-n7-log"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalisation states and checks that, among all configurations of seven distinct points on the unit
  sphere S^2, the regular pentagonal bipyramid uniquely minimises the logarithmic energy, up to orthogonal
  transformations and relabelling (Conjecture 1 of Armentano et al., J. Symbolic Comput. 137 (2026)); Comparator and
  the independent checker nanoda accept it. The same is stated and checked for the Riesz s = 2 energy, and, as a
  second check of H. Tran's Lean theorem, with this repository's own certificates, for the Coulomb energy; and for the
  Riesz s-energy for every real s with 1/3 <= s <= 7/4 (riesz_range/; Comparator, run without a sandbox and with
  prebuilt imports, and nanoda accept it). AI-produced, not peer reviewed. The repository also contains the exact certificates with independent checkers.
keywords:
  - Thomson problem
  - logarithmic energy
  - Riesz energy
  - Coulomb energy
  - pentagonal bipyramid
  - computer-assisted mathematics
  - Riesz s-energy
  - Lean 4
license: Apache-2.0
